  "metadata_synthesis": "Groundbreaking 90s British crime drama. A psychological whydunnit. Anchored by a brilliant, self-destructive forensic psychologist.",
  "setting_and_subculture": "Post-industrial 1990s Manchester. Working-class grit. The lingering decay of Thatcherism. Police stations, bleak interrogation rooms, grim crime scenes.",
  "visual_tone_and_feel": "Drab, gray, and visceral. Shadows cling to corners. A grounded, unglamorous reality. Smoky, claustrophobic spaces reflecting internal chaos.",
  "media_era_tone": "Raw mid-90s edge. Pre-CSI psychological depth. Defiant against cozy procedurals. An uncompromising look at trauma.",
  "pacing_and_structure": "Theatrical, pressure-cooker momentum. Centers on the battle of wits in the interrogation room. Slow-burn tension exploding into violent psychological breakdowns.",
  "atmosphere_and_mood": "Oppressive, fatalistic, and deeply cynical. Punctuated by flashes of pitch-black humor. A suffocating sense of guilt and consequence.",
  "themes_and_messages": "The fragility of the human mind. Deep-seated class trauma. Racism, misogyny, and systemic failure. Brilliant dysfunction masquerading as authority.",
  "character_relationships": "Combative and toxic. Fitz operates as a disruptive force against rigid police hierarchy. A deeply flawed family man failing his loved ones. Intense, twisted bonds with the killers he hunts.",
  "lead_character_type": "The self-destructive anti-hero. Obese, alcoholic, chain-smoking gambler. A genius mind drowning in self-loathing. The ultimate flawed savior.",
  "story_and_plot_type": "Psychological procedural. The 'whydunnit'. Criminal profiling driven by character, not just evidence. Confronting the roots of monstrous behavior.",
  "who_and_when": "Adult audiences. Crime drama purists. 1990s UK. Viewers drawn to complex character studies and unflinching social critique.",
  "emotional_evocation": "Visceral discomfort. Intellectual thrill. A heavy, lingering sadness for human brokenness. Morbid fascination with the criminal mind."
}
